
The name of the check-N.c file is used as a pointer to the file
../../tests/N-*.asn1. That ASN.1 file is compiled together with check-N.c
in a temporary directory. The check-N.c file contains the test engine.

For manual execution of a specific test case:

	./check-assembly.sh check-<NN>.c

check-65.c covers nested explicit and implicit BER tags on REAL aliases and
SEQUENCE members. Its complete values decode as zero (T1) and -1, +1, and +4
(T). Binary REAL contents include a format octet, an exponent, and a mantissa;
the old C0 00 and 80 00 contents omitted the mantissa and are rejection cases.
The test also checks truncated inputs and malformed tags and wrapper lengths.
The fixture was corrected after the issue #585 decoder hardening exposed it.


check-601 exercises SET CBOR maps with required and optional members, duplicate
known and unknown keys, truncated input, and malformed descriptors. Synthetic
SET extension groups and present table-selected SET open values remain
unsupported by the SET CBOR codec and are rejected.
